{
  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best unimodal result is config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 acc, with clear evidence that scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 > scgpt, multiprofile > singleprofile, and avgpool > transformer. Image alone (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 0.208. The critical open question is whether multimodal fusion can surpass the best RNA-only result, and whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L vs ResNet50) changes the picture. This experiment (config_036) pairs the best-supported RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) with the strongest available image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) and a standard concat fusion. It directly tests whether adding a powerful visual signal to the dominant RNA signal yields a meaningful gain over 0.650. If it does, subsequent experiments can explore fusion strategy and image encoder trade-offs; if it does not, the budget is better spent refining RNA-only designs. This is the highest-information experiment because it resolves the single most consequential design decision (unimodal vs. multimodal) using the strongest available components on each side."
}

